<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Anglo-Sikh War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a>–<a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> War was fought in 1848–1849 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> and the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>. It was triggered by uprisings at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/multan">Multan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazara">Hazara</a>. It ended with the annexation of the entire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-dalhousie">Lord Dalhousie</a>, ending the Sikh Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-anglo-sikh-war.jpg" alt="Second Anglo-Sikh War" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J. Harris after H. Martens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Gujrat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Second Anglo-Sikh War</b> (1848–1849), triggered by risings at Multan and Hazara, ended with Lord Dalhousie's annexation of the entire Punjab on 29 March 1849, and the young Maharaja Duleep Singh was pensioned off and later taken to England.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The British confirmed the jagir in 1846, but Raja Umed Singh joined the rising of the hill chiefs during the <b>Second Anglo-Sikh War</b> in 1848, and his lands were confiscated in 1849.</blockquote><a href="/state/jaswan-state">Jaswan State</a></li></ul></section>
